 "eng1c_vs_eng1d": {
  "question": "StudyPOL6 Part A derived 40 to 48 % of ENG1c piece steps carrying other prefill tokens, while StudyENG1d measured 0 of 248 in-window arrivals admitted into a piece's step. Which is right, and does bytes versus cached references explain it?",
